{
	title: 'Noninterrupting /plugin-sync review session and discrepancy indicator',
	spec: `/plugin-sync opens or focuses a dedicated scripted hal/plugin-sync session for the invoking terminal's client/host pair, using no provider or tokens. Startup comparison (task zh7) never switches focus or opens a modal: normal startup lands where the user expects. A persistent compact terminal status indicator says Plugins differ (N) — /plugin-sync until discrepancies are resolved or ignored. Announce newly discovered discrepancies through the existing notice line/stack without permanently crowding out errors. Reconnection or repeated detection does not duplicate notices, sessions or questions. Opening the review is an explicit user action; subsequent changes update it without stealing focus. Existing history and question mechanisms render the scripted session; no new dialog framework.

For each differing portable plugin show filename, client/server identities, readable full diff, recorded dates, ancestry/divergence status and whether either side is missing. Offer Use client version, Use server version, and Keep separate — ignore sync for <filename> on this client. Explain which file will be replaced or deleted before confirmation. Preselect the later timestamp if present and unequal, without implying that divergence is safe to overwrite. Missing and empty files remain distinct. Esc defers without writing, deleting or ignoring anything; the discrepancy remains discoverable. Keep separate uses task zh7's client-side .syncignore policy. Recheck versions when answered and show a revised comparison if either side changed. Report success only after the destination acknowledges the applied update; lifecycle notices follow task b66. Disconnected endpoints cannot complete a pending transfer; show why and allow review after reconnect.

This is a terminal feature. Web gets a discrepancy indicator only if existing shared code supplies it with zero additional work; add no web-specific UI, features or exceptions. Keep config sync and automation deferred. Demonstrate the end-to-end flow with portable keybinding overrides and two different shipped theme selections (task 4c1), including keeping them separate; do not commit real user settings. Verify no startup focus theft with many tabs, discoverability from another tab, Esc deferral, repeat-command focus, ignored-file removal from the count and stale-answer refresh.`,
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['zh7', '4c1', 'b66', 'ty', 'w4'],
	foldInto: ['an']
}
